From 71631ef2046445f1ebe2854d819c9a1487a5dd37 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 03:14:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat: franchise locations in Campaign 3 (identity key,
 city line, per-domain throttle)

Owner decision 2026-11-25: independently owned franchise offices are in the
ScaleLab ICP; they share one mail domain per brand.

- staffing-franchise.js: shared franchise domains, identity keys
  (brand+owner, brand+territory), the per-domain daily throttle and batch
  interleaving.
- Import: a shared franchise domain is never deduped as one company. It needs
  owner_approved_franchise and row.franchise {brand, owner_key, territory,
  city}; the same owner or office already in ScaleLab, or repeated in the
  batch, is refused. The identity is sealed into the profile.
- Profile: optional franchise fields, present and digested only on a
  franchise profile; every existing profile keeps its fields and digest.
- Copy v2: COPY_C city form "Saw your {{franchise_city}} office places
  {{specialty_line}}."; a franchise lead never gets the brand-name fallback.
- Send path: at most 10 sends per shared franchise domain per Vancouver day
  across every inbox and step, slot taken inside deliverOrdinaryColdStep
  before any Gmail probe or reservation; fails closed without a throttle.
  Step-1 franchise leads are interleaved in the sender assignment.

Tests: test/staffing-franchise.test.js (11). Full suite: 3666 pass, 4 fail
(the pre-existing DST/date-sensitive tests).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
